&lt;p&gt;Senior Data Engineer, Proprietary Research&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;London&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Career with Point72&#39;s Market Intelligence team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On our proprietary research team—Market Intelligence— you will uncover insights about markets and the broader economy through deep compliant fundamental research and applying data science and engineering techniques to alternative data sets. In partnership with our investment professionals and Compliance team, our team of analysts, data scientists and engineers work together to produce compliant research and build tools that inform our firm’s investments. We look for other bright, motivated, and collaborative people to join our team and grow with us—a majority of the leaders in our group were promoted from within.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with investment professionals, researchers, and data scientists to design, build, and launch robust end-to-end business solutions including data pipelines, products and tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop big data processing pipelines including but not limited to ingestion, transformation, trends creation to deliver AI-ready data assets &amp;amp; products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reusable software components, libraries, and APIs that enable rapid experimentation and production deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement data quality, lineage, and governance controls to ensure datasets are reliable, auditable, and compliant with compliance policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable AI-native cloud-based infrastructure using distributed systems techniques, to deliver efficient data-driven business solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize performance, cost, and reliability of software systems through benchmarking and iterative improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT’S REQUIRED&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in Data Engineering, Software Engineering or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of strong experience in Python development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with system design and leading multi-person development efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with distributed data processing frameworks like Spark&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with building scalable APIs, and software applications w/ focus on backend infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud platforms and services for data storage and compute (for example AWS, Google Cloud Platform, or Azure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with orchestration technologies like Airflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of/experience with langraph/langchain or similar frameworks, embedding models, vector, graph databases is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong drive to staying current with AI advancements and translating emerging techniques into practical, real-world applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We take care of our people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our people, their careers, their health, and their well-being. When you work here, we provide:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical and Dental Insurances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous parental and family leave policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support for employee-led affinity groups representing women, people of colour and the LGBQT+ community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental and physical wellness programmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-contributory pension and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Point72&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry&#39;s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people&#39;s long-term growth. For more information, visit https://point72.com/&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title: Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;London/Hybrid&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;Type: &lt;/strong&gt;Full-time&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level: &lt;/strong&gt;Mid Level&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: EMS&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Engineering Lead&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Elwood&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Elwood Technologies is a FCA regulated firm that provides end-to-end digital asset Execution Management, and Risk Management Software to institutional clients. We are now looking for a Software Engineer to work on our EMS platform within the Engineering Team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly skilled Golang &lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team responsible for designing, building, and optimising a next-generation multi-region, multi-tenanted Execution Management System (EMS) platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have experience building concurrent, performance sensitive systems where correctness and high availability are maintained across multiple regions to meet the stringent demands of our global trading customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Development: &lt;/strong&gt;Design and implement low-latency, high-throughput systems for a multi-region, multi-tenanted EMS platform, ensuring compliance with industry standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Latency Optimisation: &lt;/strong&gt;Analyse and optimise critical paths in the system to reduce latency and improve performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distributed Systems: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain distributed, fault-tolerant systems with high availability across multiple regions, ensuring data consistency and low-latency communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitoring &amp;amp; Observability: &lt;/strong&gt;Implement real-time monitoring, telemetry and alerting systems for proactive issue detection and resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with product, QA and infrastructure teams to align technical solutions with business requirements and ensure seamless deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code reviews:&lt;/strong&gt; Review teammates&#39; code with rigour and help raise the team&#39;s collective standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Assisted Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Use AI coding assistants heavily and critically - catching what they get wrong is part of the job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications / Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years professional backend engineering, including concurrent, performance sensitive systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on production &lt;strong&gt;GOLANG &lt;/strong&gt;expertise. You should be able to walk through a non-trivial Go system you built and defend its design. C++ or Rust experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;distributed systems&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;event-driven architectures&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g. Nats, Aeron)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;multi-tenancy patterns&lt;/strong&gt; and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud platforms (e.g. AWS, GCP, Azure) and tools for &lt;strong&gt;multi-region deployments&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working knowledge of databases and caches (PostgreSQL, SQLite, Redis, Zookeeper).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with observability tools (e.g. Prometheus, Grafana, ELK stack).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills, with a track record of working in cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail and ability to work under pressure in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of crypto markets and products (Desirable).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in leveraging LLMs to accelerate delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial Services experience is desired along with a background in trading/EMS platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💵&amp;nbsp; Competitive salary and compensation packages&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍎 Fully paid medical and discounted dental schemes for employees and their family&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;✈️ Generous time off + bank holidays&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍼 Enhanced parental leave for all employees who have been with the company for one (1) year&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🍔 Modern offices with snacks and a weekly Ubereats allowance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💪 Free onsite gym&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🐕‍ Employee Assistance Programme&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 Paid study leave and personal leave&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Elwood?&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join a series A FinTech company&amp;nbsp; and help shape the future of finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A startup with deep financial backing and a strong market presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our platform is enabling institutional access to the most exciting growth opportunity in Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a modern technology stack and help solve high impact problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong client focused team with a diverse background&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re a Global company and have modern, centrally based offices in London, New York and Singapore.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weekly office requirement:&lt;/strong&gt; Monday/Wednesday weekly &lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment type:&lt;/strong&gt; Permanent&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seniority level: &lt;/strong&gt;Mid-senior&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At GWI we’re always looking for extraordinary people who thrive on making an extraordinary impact. Right now we’re looking for a&lt;strong&gt; Product Manager &lt;/strong&gt;to play a key role in our &lt;strong&gt;User Management (Revenue&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;amp; Enablement) &lt;/strong&gt;team in &lt;strong&gt;London&lt;/strong&gt;. If that’s you, and making a difference gets you out of bed in the morning, keep reading. It could be the start of something, well, extraordinary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Sounds great, what will I be doing? 🤔&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Product Manager you&#39;ll own the systems that make GWI&#39;s subscription and consumption business run, such as billing, metering, user plans, feature access, product analytics and user messaging. It&#39;s the layer everything else sits on. Get it right and GWI can price, package and sell in new ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two big pieces of work sit at the heart of this role. The first is billing for our consumption products, which is an area we&#39;re actively developing, and one you&#39;ll help shape. The second is making our internal tools talk to each other properly, so user data flows consistently between them and Salesforce, and everyone across the business is working from the same picture. Most of your stakeholders are internal - Revenue Operations, Finance, Business Intelligence, Client Success and Engineering - with some direct client contact along the way. You&#39;ll lead one squad of front-end and back-end engineers and a designer, alongside the PM and Engineers in our sister squad, Identity &amp;amp; Access - together you cover the whole of User Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A few things you’ll be responsible for:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;👉 Connecting our internal user management tools with Salesforce and each other, so data flows consistently and user information is mapped the same way everywhere
&lt;p&gt;👉 Billing for our consumption products - metering, API usage, payment flows and user plans&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 Customer feature flags, access and management - who can see what, and why&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 Product analytics - event firing, sign-up flow data, usage data - so the business can see what&#39;s happening and act on it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 Building the roadmap from client feedback, internal stakeholder input and usage analytics, and prioritising the most valuable work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 Scoping the work and owning how your squad delivers it&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;It’s also fun; shaking things up is what working for GWI is all about. You’ll need to be flexible, comfortable with continuous change, and working in a high-tempo environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What do I need to bring with me? 🧳&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll need to be able to demonstrate the core skills this role requires. You don&#39;t have to tick all the boxes right away; the important thing is that you’re willing to learn. Here’s what the team will be looking for in you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 You&#39;ve shipped products at a B2B company&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 You&#39;ve built complex roadmaps with cross-functional dependencies, and you can balance multiple priorities without losing the plot&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 You make informed decisions at pace, even when the picture isn&#39;t complete&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 You&#39;re a strong problem solver, negotiator and influencer — you get alignment without needing authority&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 You explain complex things clearly to very different audiences: execs, engineers, customers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 You ask questions and draw knowledge out of your team to find the right engineering and design solutions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 You make informed decisions at pace, even when the picture isn&#39;t complete, and you&#39;re happy taking a big initiative and running with it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 Bonus points if you&#39;ve worked with Salesforce before, or with tools that need to sync data between systems and internal user management systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Equally important is attitude. We want people who think big (to make an impact), ask why (to find a better way), and show respect (to everyone, at every level, all the time). Those are our values, and they’re a big part of what we’re looking for in you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 You&#39;ll work on how GWI packages its consumption products - commercial problems with real weight behind them&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 Your squad owns infrastructure the whole company depends on, so the work gets noticed&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 You&#39;ll build relationships across the business, from Finance to Engineering to the Exec team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 You&#39;ll learn from a senior PM who knows this space, with room to run your own squad your way&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Diversity, Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion 🫶&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity is fundamental to who we are—as a data company and as a workplace. Our data reflects global realities, and so must our teams. We strive to build a workforce as diverse and inclusive as the insights we deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Disability Confident employer, we welcome applications from disabled candidates and are committed to making adjustments throughout the hiring process—whether that&#39;s extra time, materials in advance or a different format, breaks, an adjusted interview format, assistive tools, or flexible scheduling. We&#39;re happy to discuss whatever would work best for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We actively encourage applications from underrepresented and marginalised communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At GWI, you&#39;ll find a place to contribute meaningfully, grow professionally, and belong fully.&lt;/p&gt;
