&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRINCIPAL COMPLIANCE OFFICER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UK financial crime program is being built now, and it has to stand up to the FCA. This role sits in Compliance, reports to the US BSA/AML Officer, and owns the UK framework end to end — AML/CTF, sanctions, fraud, ABC, KYC/CDD/EDD, transaction monitoring, SARs, and the operating rhythm. You will still work the hard cases. It is a builder seat with accountability, not a queue job with “strategy” in the title.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have eight or more years inside an FCA-regulated bank, EMI, PI, or payments firm, have owned or rebuilt a financial crime control framework, and can still open a file, this is the seat. You will build the UK program from the ground up, setting the standards the team and the FCA will use. This is consumer-scale payments financial crime work – not a private-banking book – and you’ll sit directly with Product and Engineering. You’ll operate in a small team with a direct line to the US BSA/AML Officer, where scope is broad and process is lean. The measure of success is a program that still works a year later, and the role sits alongside MLRO / SMF17-adjacent duties for the UK entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run the UK financial crime programme: policy, procedures, CDD/EDD, risk rating, sanctions screening, transaction monitoring, SAR handling, escalation, QA, and training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn MLR 2017, POCA, the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act, JMLSG, the FCA Financial Crime Guide, SYSC 6.3, and payments/EMI expectations into something operations and product can run&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the UK business-wide risk assessment and keep it honest as the product, customer mix, and channels change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle complex cases — PEPs, adverse media, sanctions hits, high-risk onboarding, fraud typologies, escalations — then use the queue to fix the framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up first- and second-line controls: documentation, workflows, vendor oversight, quality sampling, MI, and issue management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Put UK requirements into the customer journey with Legal, Operations, Product, and Engineering. Be the UK voice in global design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on quality, residual risk, throughput, and control health, and prepare the program for internal audit, skilled-person reviews, and FCA scrutiny&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the operating model as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach, and set the standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support MLRO / SMF17-adjacent duties as the UK permissions model requires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASiC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of hands-on experience with financial crime in a regulated UK firm (bank, EMI, PI, payments, or e-money), including substantial KYC/CDD/EDD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will still do the cases, close gaps in a small team, do not wait for a 30-page RACI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know the UK regime well enough to argue a point — MLR 2017, JMLSG, POCA, UK sanctions, FCA expectations — and how it lands in a payments product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have designed or rebuilt a framework, procedure, or control, not only cleared files or written a policy nobody ran&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have led people or a workstream. You can defend a risk decision and explain it to the Product without jargon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU financial crime experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the EU AML package, 6AMLD, EBA guidelines, national transposition, or an EU FIU/regulator, especially on cross-border payments, wallets, or EMI/PI products (useful because X Money will not stay inside one perimeter)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office five days a week; occasional work-from-home when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base + equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UK private medical covering GPs and specialists; pension; life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days’ paid time off; lunch and dinner allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Cato Networks is the converged network and security cloud for the AI era.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;As AI reshapes cybersecurity, enterprises face a dual challenge: unlocking AI’s potential while defending against AI-driven attacks. Cato addresses both through a unified, cloud-native platform, providing the visibility and context to prioritize risks and stop threats in real time across users, applications, data, and AI agents.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Join us as we scale: take on ambitious technological challenges and shape the next generation of enterprise security at a company trusted by thousands of organizations worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking a Commercial Account Executive who is eager to drive growth within the Mid-Market Public Sector segment. If you’re excited about connecting with Local Authorities, City Halls, Healthcar providers/Emergency Services, solving problems, and delivering cutting-edge solutions, we’d love to have you on our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Sales Cycle: &lt;/strong&gt;Manage the entire sales process for Mid-Market Public Sector accounts, from lead generation to closing, ensuring customers receive real value from our solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage with Decision-Makers: &lt;/strong&gt;Reach out to key business decision-makers (CEOs, CTOs, IT Directors) to understand their challenges and align our cybersecurity and SaaS offerings to meet their needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Focus on Customer Success: &lt;/strong&gt;Help SMB and mid-market businesses grow securely by positioning our solutions as critical to their long-term success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage Shorter Sales Cycles: &lt;/strong&gt;Navigate faster-paced sales cycles, building relationships and managing multiple opportunities while driving results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Approach: &lt;/strong&gt;Leverage CRM data, sales tools, and metrics to track performance, refine strategies, and optimize outreach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate with the Team: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with your colleagues, sharing tips, strategies, and best practices to drive success across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expand Market Reach: &lt;/strong&gt;Build strong partnerships with local MSSPs, VARs, and other key stakeholders to bring our solutions to more SMB and mid-market organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay Ahead of the Curve: &lt;/strong&gt;Stay updated on the latest trends in cybersecurity and SaaS, positioning yourself as a valuable resource to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: 3-5 years of experience in inside sales within cybersecurity, SaaS, or related industries, with proven success in managing sales cycles and engaging with decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Success&lt;/strong&gt;: A demonstrated history of consistently meeting or exceeding sales quotas and driving revenue growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;: Strong understanding of cybersecurity, SaaS, or networking solutions and ideally you will have worked within UGAP/CANUT frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship-Driven&lt;/strong&gt;: Ability to build long-term, trust-based relationships with key stakeholders and decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative&lt;/strong&gt;: Experience working with partners, MSSPs, VARs, and other strategic collaborators to drive sales and expand business opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
